@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "FAQ";
}

<h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

<hr/>

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-12">
        <div class="card">
            <h5 class="card-header">Q: What does the privacy option on the game mean?</h5>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p>When you create a game you are given the option if the game should be 'publicly' listed. This means that:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>The game may be listed on the homepage as a featured game (TODO)</li>
                    <li>The game may be listed on other areas of the website (TODO)</li>
                    <li>The usernames of the game participants (<strong>not emails</strong>) will be visible. Unless overridden in the users profile. (TODO)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row" style="padding-top: 20px;">
    <div class="col-12">
        <div class="card">
            <h5 class="card-header">Q: What are the different 'Scrabble' boards?</h5>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p>When you are creating a game you are provided some different options for the board. You can read a detailed breakdown of the differences <a asp-area="" asp-controller="About" asp-action="ScrabbleGames">here</a>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row" style="padding-top: 20px;">
    <div class="col-12">
        <div class="card">
            <h5 class="card-header">Q: Is this website free? will I ever have to pay money?</h5>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p>
                    This website is currently provided free of charge and there are no limitations on accounts. There is undoubtedly a commercial viability to a website such as this and there will be a transition at some point to move to a subscription model.
                </p>
                <p>
                    However that being said; even with a future subscription model there is an expectation that users will be able to play games for free to some extent. That is yet to be decided.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@section Styles {

    <link href="~/css/faq.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
}